Khronos OpenCL(TM) API headers - fetched at build time from public upstream when
no OpenCL headers are installed on the build host.

Component:   OpenCL-Headers (cl.h, cl_gl.h, cl_version.h, cl_platform.h,
             cl_ext.h)
Upstream:    https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenCL-Headers
Version:     pinned by the commit in tools/unitrace/scripts/get_cl_headers.py,
             the single source of truth (not repeated here)
License:     Apache-2.0 (see ./LICENSE)

How it is used: cmake/OpenCL.cmake uses the host's OpenCL headers if found;
otherwise scripts/get_cl_headers.py clones OpenCL-Headers at the pinned commit
and copies the headers into the build tree. Either way unitrace compiles
against the Khronos API headers.

To bump: update the commit in get_cl_headers.py, refresh LICENSE from upstream
at the new commit, and update tools/unitrace/third-party-programs.txt if the
license or copyright changed.
